        ep = export(TestModule(), (torch.randn(4, 4),), strict=False)
This errors with:
  File "/data/users/tmanlaibaatar/pytorch/torch/nn/modules/container.py", line 141, in __getitem__
    return self.__class__(OrderedDict(list(self._modules.items())[idx]))
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
TypeError: _ModuleStackTracer.__init__.<locals>.AttrProxy.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'path'

The reason is when we run non-strict tracing, we replace all submodules with a attribute proxy to track the nn_module_stack. But in our library code, we try to recreate a submodule via self.class which causes the tracer to create a new attr proxy for it.
